WEBVTT

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.580
It's gotten kinda chilly, hasn't it?

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.830
Um, what is this passage?

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.460
You've got eyes, don't you?
It's underground.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.550
We use it for prisoner transport.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.380
Uh-huh...

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.890
I don't need to hear
torture screams right now!

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.720
What? It's daytime?!

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.940
Despite all the talk of realism,
they sped time up! Shitty game!

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:49.360
This mansion belongs to Her Highness
Queen Govern, ruler of the Closed City.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.000
The Tribulation of a Killer

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.260
Esteemed City Guard Captain
Tesla currently also resides here.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.510
The likes of you would ordinarily
never be permitted inside.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.640
This limited <i>exception </i>is
under Captain Tesla's orders.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:46.650
The noble figure seated
there is Captain Tesla.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.820
Do show proper respect.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.400
Come. Sit.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:58.240
I expect you are hungry. Dine with me.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.910
R-Right. Thanks.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.750
If I sit on this fancy chair
with these pee pants...

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.210
"You reek of urine!"

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.960
...won't that be the outcome here?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.760
This isn't how I imagined
the City Guard Captain...

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:20.760
Um... why did you suddenly summon me here?

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.560
I'm telling you! It's the pee!

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.140
Peeing yourself was a special trick!

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.640
Just ignore Reona.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.520
I heard Martin's sister's side,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.190
but people who intend to kill
don't use fruit knives to do it.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.280
T-That's right!

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.870
Well, Alicia is currently attempting
to kill me with fruit knives, though.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:46.370
During my visit to the scene, I noticed
you had a sword you could have used.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.250
A sword? There really was one...

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.960
Besides, the knife had
pierced through his throat.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:58.880
Even a knife master would struggle to
get a knife into the back of the throat.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.930
Therefore I determined it was
a sudden, unforeseen accident.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.140
What is it? Did you pee again?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.940
Oh, I've finally met a person in this
shitty game whose head is on straight!

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.360
Though it's an NPC and not a person.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.480
And so, Hiro, you are acquitted.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.610
Th-Thank you so much!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.490
I'm sorry for imprisoning you.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.860
Now, please dig in.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.370
Yes! Gladly!

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.370
So good! The taste feature is awesome!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.580
But do watch out for Martin's sister.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.380
She appears to still harbor
resentment toward you.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.510
Should you have a problem, come see me.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.630
That is, if you would like some help.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:44.300
From the Ted City Guard Captain,
"Thundering Tesla."

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.810
Wow! Sounds like a
potential party member flag!

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:48.890
Hiro, it's just obligatory politeness.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.560
What? Is it?!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.150
Well, whatever the case may be...

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.650
I've been acquitted!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.110
No more sneaking around in a hood!

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.280
I can finally have a normal adventure!

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.620
For the time being, I'll head to
my house to retrieve my sword.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:09.410
Did you go pee?
Do you need to poop? Are you thirsty?

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.330
Hey! Stop that!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.210
I'm not a child on his
way to kindergarten!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.010
Your house is on the outskirts
of town, so it's pretty far.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:21.840
Be vigilant on the way there. Got it?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.340
I know!

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.600
There's also the matter of Alicia.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.140
But I've been cleared now, so--

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.930
Oh, if it isn't Hiro!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.680
I heard you were cleared.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.230
That's right!

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.850
Ugh, are you kidding me?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.860
<i>I </i>think he murdered the guy.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:36.730
Huh?

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.780
Yes. I think so, too.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.690
He has the face of a killer!

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:41.990
Whoa!

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:46.240
Don't think your acquittal gets you
off the hook, you filthy criminal!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.620
Hey! Wait! Sto--

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.210
Yeah, you better run!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.960
You know, you really
are fast runner, Hiro.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.340
What the hell? I was cleared of charges!

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:04.550
Even though you were cleared, public
opinion is harsh. That's realism for you!

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.430
I could do without it!

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.680
That bastard won't get off that easily!

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.770
They're still looking for me.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:17.150
We can't get back to your house
without crossing that bridge.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:20.110
Looks like we can't get
your sword for a while.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.360
Nothing's changed
about my situation at all!

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.370
Well, at least the City Guard
won't chase you anymore!

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.030
How about we acquire
some items while we wait?

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.040
Items?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:34.620
Your childhood friend is gunning for you,
so some smoke bombs would be good!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.380
How much do you have?

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.250
That'll only get you a single herb.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.130
The ones that take days to work?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.930
Say, how <i>do </i>you make money in KQ anyway?

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.050
That's the same as real life, too!

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.680
Work, borrow, or steal!

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.980
Steal?!

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:56.900
Look, there's a couple of easy marks!

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.820
You mean <i>robbery</i>?! Are you crazy?

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.780
No more run-ins with the law!

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:08.530
So then work it is?
It'll take time, though.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:14.580
Well, I'm used to fetch quests and
errands from other full-dive RPGs...

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.040
All right! I'll give it a shot!

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.380
This is it, Hiro.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:24.290
Employment Agency

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:24.470
Don't jobs normally come from,
like, a guild or something?

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.800
This is a back-alley job office!

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.430
"Back-alley"?! What do you mean?

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.720
Though you've been acquitted,
public opinion is still harsh.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.020
So this place is perfect!

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.310
It's a back-alley office for people
who've become unemployable.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.520
A <i>shady </i>place to introduce
<i>shady </i>jobs to <i>shady </i>people!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.190
That's a lot of "shady"s...

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.160
Hm?

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:54.080
Hmph. The murderer wants a job?

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.790
I'm not a murderer! I'm innocent!

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:00.420
Yeah, right. You must have
paid a fortune to the Guard.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.170
Dammit! She doesn't believe me at all!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:08.300
Well, no matter. I have jobs
that will even take a murderer.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:15.390
"Hard labor at an underground work camp.
Duration: one month. Reward: 20,000 gald."

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.770
Smoke bombs don't cost that much, right?

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.940
Probably about 20 or 30 gald.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:25.980
Um, do you have something less intense?
With a slightly shorter duration?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:29.610
Ugh. A picky killer, I see.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:33.700
"Do what Brian asks for one hour.
Reward: 100 gald."

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.790
Oh, I might take this!

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:39.460
Then go to the extravagant home
in the northeast part of town.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:45.750
Then I just do what Brian asks me to do?
Like wash dishes or pull weeds?

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.220
Here's a whip. Take it with you.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.760
A whip? For livestock?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.510
It's for Brian.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.930
Brian is a middle-aged man who
likes being struck while naked.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.310
Huh? Wha--? What was that?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:06.280
Oh, come on. You're gonna do whatever
that super masochist, Brian, asks.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.150
I mean, do I have to spell it out for you?

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.780
Then let's be on our way
to Mr. Brian's house!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:12.990
Hell no!

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.450
You can't buy smoke bombs
if you don't, though.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.990
I don't need 'em that bad!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.660
Whip some naked old coot,
then it's "quest complete"?!

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:22.370
The <i>hell </i>kind of quest is <i>that</i>?!

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.500
Get off your high horse!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.050
Everyone's doing their damnedest working
these jobs in the shadows and margins!

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:33.640
Everybody's desperately hoping that
one day, they too can live a normal life!

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.890
No, I, uh... the thing is...

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:39.850
Get out, you lousy murderer!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.310
She got really mad...

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.650
That NPC's backstory is that
she opened the back-alley job office

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.700
using money she earned from
underground labor in her youth.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.120
She must have felt you
were mocking her and her life.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.740
Tell me this stuff sooner!

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:01.370
That wasn't my intention at all!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:05.170
You don't have the guts to steal
or appreciate the value of work...

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:07.210
That just leaves borrowing.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.510
Those are some sharp and biting words.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:11.920
Wait. Borrow? From who?

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.380
Who else?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:19.100
A certain player character who's doing
whatever he wants and ignoring the story.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.850
I'm really not a fan of Ginji.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.650
Me neither.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:30.400
But we have to be practical
about our situation.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.650
"Practical," huh?

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.370
Huh?

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:39.620
Oh, it's the jiggly, jiggly fairy.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.660
It's been a while.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:47.670
Ginji, how have you been?
Ever decide to try to beat the game?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.960
Nah. I'm over that.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.880
So, what brings you here?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.680
Well, I was hoping
you'd help this player out.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.550
Hello again.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.930
Oh, it's you! Does this mean
you endured the torture?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.930
How dare you ask like it's
no big deal?! Whose fault--

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.100
No, he didn't!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:08.520
Actually, he peed himself
while being tortured.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.270
And then they let him go!

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.440
Hey! Reona!

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:16.070
So they let you go if you piss yourself?

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.450
Isn't that funny?

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.870
It's not funny at all!

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:24.330
Hiro, we're trying to
open a dialogue here.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.000
You could skip that part!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.420
Stop chuckling!
You sold me out to the guards!

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.000
It's all your fault!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.010
What's with that look?

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:36.930
It's thanks to me you got to be acquitted!

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:38.930
Show some gratitude, idiot!

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:42.350
This asshole seriously pisses me off!

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.850
So, Miss Jiggly? What did you want?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:51.320
Well, you see, I was hoping
you'd lend him some money.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.980
Lend money to this mouthy brat?

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:59.070
I ain't giving you squat.
Bug off, piss boy.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.950
P-Piss... boy?

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.410
What did you just say?!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:11.000
Now, Ginji, Hiro here is no piss boy!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.840
Stay out of this, Reona!

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.550
He's the "Nice Shower Best Friend Killer"!

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:18.970
Holy hell, <i>please </i>stop talking!

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:22.930
I don't care what he's called.
I ain't lending him money.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:27.020
Now buzz off! Before
the booze reeks like piss!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.730
What's the big idea, piss boy?

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.240
I...

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.700
Bastard!

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.620
I...

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.250
Hiro!

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.420
I-I'm doing it again! Calm down!

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.210
What if he ends up like Martin?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.210
Do it! Get him!

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.010
It's emotional battle time!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.170
What the hell is wrong with her?!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.720
You stupid brat!

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.640
I'll choke you out!

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.980
Quit squirming around, bastard!

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:09.850
Can it, you drunk!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.480
All right! It's just like a fantasy game!

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:14.480
In what way?!

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:18.360
Screw it! I'm using my secret weapon!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.490
Oh, shit.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:25.950
Is it magic? Is he gonna
hit me with magic?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:26.790
What?

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:30.330
Brass knuckles! A classic gangster weapon!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.330
This screams fantasy!

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:34.880
Again, how does this scream fantasy?!

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:40.970
Ow! Ow! Ow! I'll go bald!

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.510
You'll pull my hair out!

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.180
Let go!

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.970
You deserve it for trying
to punch me with that!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.220
Hey, ow!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.640
Let go!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.600
<i>You </i>let go!

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.020
Ow! Ow!

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.650
I-I'm gonna go bald!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.570
Ah! My gout!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.790
Take this, asshole!

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:13.040
Hiro...

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:19.510
Are you going to injure
someone in a rage again?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.130
Forgive me, Martin!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.720
What's wrong, Hiro?

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:25.800
It's Martin!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:29.180
He should be dead, but he's here!

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:32.560
H-Huh?

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:33.850
He's gone?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.810
The timing with the ghosts is irregular.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:40.900
Sometimes they disappear immediately, and
sometimes they stick around a few minutes.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.900
Well, regardless, you'll get used to it.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.570
H-Hell no!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.120
I do <i>not </i>wanna get used to this.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.080
Speak of the devil.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.500
Here come mine now.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.540
Look, I just don't know.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:03.130
I'll never figure out
the answer to your question.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:08.010
Deep down, Ginji might
regret what he did, too.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.970
Regret it?

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.850
Yes, regret killing his friend characters.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:17.810
Maybe that's why he
kept playing this game.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:23.030
The persistent feeling
of guilt from killing...

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:27.030
Is that another aspect of KQ's realism?

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:29.950
Ginji.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:30.700
Yeah?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:33.700
I'm sorry... for the way I acted.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:37.330
So some people do snap for
real even though it's a game.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.340
Huh? Y-You snapped, too!

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:46.720
I haven't been that worked up in a long
time. Maybe you had an effect on me.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:53.100
I guess that's... youth for you.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.360
Ginji?

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.150
What is it? Let me sleep now, will ya?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.700
Thank goodness. I thought you'd died.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:11.160
Like I'd die from just
having my hair pulled. Dummy.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.160
Ginji, aren't you forgetting something?

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.790
You failed to beat Hiro in a duel!

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.540
As agreed, we're taking
every coin you've got!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.830
Huh?

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.960
Oh, right.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.590
Here.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:29.090
Th-There was no such agreement!
We only came here to borrow money!

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.510
And what's this about a duel?
Rotten opportunist.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.520
Hiro, that battle was great!

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:41.230
You defeated a boss you couldn't
beat before! A true RPG experience!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:44.980
It doesn't feel like an RPG to me at all.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.860
Th-This is...

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.700
"Elder-Hunting Best Friend Killer:

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.200
Amicide Who Robs Old Men"?!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.700
What? Why?!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.000
I did no such thing!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:03.130
You <i>did </i>pick a fight with an old guy and
ultimately take his money. The shoe fits.

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.920
You're the one who took his money! Not me!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:11.050
Now, now. We got money
and a new title. It's all good.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:14.390
Come on. Let's get the smoke bombs!

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:17.470
Hiro, we're here.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:18.800
"Welcome to Melissa's Shop!"

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.940
They're both item shops?

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:23.610
That's right. Which do you pick?

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:27.780
Hmm. Seems kinda suspect.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.450
I pick this one.

